# Touch rules

Before writing code, read [`context/TAME_GUIDANCE.md`](../../context/TAME_GUIDANCE.md) and the
specific living rule named by [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md). Before writing a session record,
read [`.claude/rules/session-logs.md`](../../.claude/rules/session-logs.md) and
[`.claude/rules/session-log-provenance.md`](../../.claude/rules/session-log-provenance.md).

Docs and implementation stay synchronized: if a touched document cites a path, command, witness,
or behavior, check that target and update the citation in the same change when it moves. Use plain
Gauge prose, bounded commands, and a named verification step. Do not silently rewrite historical
logs or fossils.
